/T (For any developer, learning low-level languages and having constraint is an enormously beneficial exercise, appreciating hardware and history more. Skills developed can be transferred to multiple sectors, such as AI, graphics, etc, to make minute optimisations for significant performance gains. This project hopes to inspire new developers to take on this challenge, learning from the past to innovate in the future. )
/E (For any developer, learning low-level languages and having constraint is an enormously beneficial exercise, appreciating hardware and history more. Skills developed can be transferred to multiple sectors, such as AI, graphics, etc, to make minute optimisations for significant performance gains. This project hopes to inspire new developers to take on this challenge, learning from the past to innovate in the future. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [0]
