/Title (Unlike its competition, which used more conventional frame buffers, the Atari 2600 has  a unique chip called the Television Interface Adapter \(TIA\) used to interface CRT TVs.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 508 0 R
/Next 542 0 R
>>
endobj
541 0 obj
<<
/Title (There are also 40 Playfield Graphics per scanline stored in only 20 bits, being the lowest resolution object, often used for walls and floors. Can be mirrored or repeated, asymmetrical fields need careful timing. Collisions between these objects are detected by the hardware, making checking trivial!)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 508 0 R
/Prev 543 0 R
>>
endobj
